--TEST--
a `fromIso` text written as a literal is read while compiling, and a text that is malformed or names no real date or time is one diagnostic at the literal (`rule:core-classes/a-time-class-builds-its-own-values` and `rule:expressions/intrinsic-constant-arguments`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $utc = Core\Time\Zone::UTC;

// A day February 2024 does not have.
var $noSuchDay = Core\Time\Date::fromIso('2024-02-30');
// An hour past the last one.
var $pastMidnight = Core\Time\TimeOfDay::fromIso('24:00');
// A month and a day without their leading zero.
var $short = Core\Time\Date::fromIso('2024-3-1');
// The ISO 8601 basic form, with no `-`.
var $basic = Core\Time\Date::fromIso('20240301');
// An offset with no zone after it.
var $offset = Core\Time\DateTime::fromIso('2024-03-01T09:30+01:00', $utc);
// A local time with no zone in the text and no second argument.
var $noZone = Core\Time\DateTime::fromIso('2024-03-01T09:30');
// An offset Vienna does not have in January.
var $wrongOffset = Core\Time\DateTime::fromIso('2026-01-05T08:30:00+02:00[Europe/Vienna]');
// The same text behind a variable is read at run time, and is not reported.
var $text = '2024-02-30';
var $later = Core\Time\Date::fromIso($text);

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: 2024-02 has no day 30
%A
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: the hour is `24`, and an hour is `00` to `23`
%A
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: the month is 2 digits, in the form `YYYY-MM-DD`
%A
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: expected `-` at byte 4, in the form `YYYY-MM-DD`
%A
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: the text has an offset and no zone. Write the zone after the offset, such as `[Europe/Vienna]`, or read the text with `Core\Time\Instant::fromIso`, then call `->in($zone)`
%A
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: the text names no zone. Write one after the time, such as `[Europe/Vienna]`, or pass `$zone`
%A
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: the zone has no offset `+02:00` at 2026-01-05T08:30:00. Its offset at that moment is `+01:00`
%A
error: aborting due to 7 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
